 "_comment": "The gate jump's camera takes (M8-T29, maintainer 2026-11-19, after show-likeness reviews; every take under 3 s). The jump is cut into short takes from these pools, picked at random per jump, never the same take twice in a row and never the last jump's opening take, and only takes whose camera stays clear of the gate, the station and the planets and can see the ship: the run-in's 'approach' takes until cut_lead_s before the ship is predicted at the mouth (M8-T18), then 'mouth' takes to the ring (a take tagged 'when': 'entry' goes on the take that holds the moment of entry, one tagged 'before' only before it; on the way back a take tagged 'after' waits 1.5 s, until the blue vortex opens); at the ring's 0.3 s flash a hard cut to the arrival side: 'arrival_open' takes from the pylons' glow, which starts at the cut, as the blue vortex opens, then 'arrival_out' takes from the moment the ship bursts out of the ring (about 1 s through the funnel) until control returns (3 s or 500 m in front of the mouth). Each take's keys run 0 to 2.9 s and it is cut at most 2.6 s in (under 3 s with the ring's 0.3 s flash); a take marked 'feature': true (an interesting angle, maintainer 2026-11-19) runs 0 to 4.9 s and is cut at most 4.6 s in. Actors: 'player' (offsets in its frame: +z behind it, +y above it) and 'gate' (its frame: -z in front of the mouth, the ship flies in along +z, the funnel runs on to about +1200). 'roll' turns the picture, degrees.",
